Type: Project
Package: pairwise.meta.analysis.app
Title: pmatools wizard (Shiny app for pairwise MA + GRADE)
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yuki", "Furukawa", email = "furukawa.y.psy@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: NOT AN R PACKAGE, AND NOT DELETABLE. This file exists so
    rsconnect can read the Imports field below and install those
    packages on the shinyapps.io server; it is a deployment manifest,
    nothing more. The real package DESCRIPTION is one directory up.
    Version above is the app's own (wizard/UI work) and deliberately
    tracks separately from the package version -- rsconnect ignores the
    field entirely. WARNING - the rare-event backends metafor, mmeta
    and BiasedUrn are referenced only as name strings in
    R/_pmatools/rare_events.R, so rsconnect's code scan cannot detect
    them; this Imports field is the ONLY thing that installs them on
    the server. Removing them deploys fine and breaks the rare-event
    method suite at runtime, in production. Never remove them (see
    deploy.R and stage_bundle.R, and ../CLAUDE.md).
